  "body": "**Replaces #432** (opened from the old fork, which can no longer take pushes). Same head commit; nothing else changed.\n\nPart of #363 (peck threading; the research comment there has the sources). Follow-up #417 (PR stacked on this one) makes the G76 output match these passes.\n\n## What changed\n**New threading op param `infeed_plan` (`turning::ThreadInfeed`).**\n- **Infeed method:** radial, modified flank at an angle θ, or alternating flank.\n- **Depth schedule:** constant depth, or constant area (first depth × √n).\n- **Minimum depth per pass, finish allowance, and spring passes** (default 0, capped at 98).\n- The existing `infeed` is the first-pass depth.\n- It's shown as rows on the op's Passes tab (`thread_infeed_page.rs`).\n\n**Kernel.** `crates/motion/src/turning/infeed.rs` lays the passes from the plan. `thread_in` calls `thread_planned_in` with the default plan.\n- **Flank:** each pass starts shifted by −(tip − root)·tan θ along its travel. Finishing and spring passes sit on the pitch lattice, so lead and spindle phase never change.\n- **Safety:** every pass stays inside the finished V exactly when θ ≤ half the insert's included angle. A larger angle is refused by name at the command (create, paste, edit, retype via `thread_gate`) and again at Generate.\n- **Alternating:** flips the side each pass.\n\n**The verdict judges the laid passes.** `the_verdict_reads_the_shifted_pass` pins a past-half-angle pass being convicted. `attach_cycle` moved to `thread_cycle.rs`.\n\n**Defaults are byte-identical.** The default plan makes the same `blade::rungs(root, ref_top, infeed, 0)` call at the same stations.\n- The op stamp includes the plan only when it isn't the default, so cached threads stay fresh.\n- The project key is written only when non-default, so there's no version rung. An older build drops a non-default plan and cuts the radial ladder; that's not a gouge.\n- No existing golden changed.\n\n`docs/decisions/416-thread-infeed.md`\n\n## How tested\n- New motion `turning_thread_infeed` (8 tests):\n  - √n depths with the minimum-depth clamp;\n  - allowance plus spring-pass count;\n  - flank shift, including the full 30°;\n  - alternating flip;\n  - verdict silent for every method × schedule on the thread fixture;\n  - a shifted pass is convicted;\n  - refusals by name.\n- New app `turning_thread_infeed` (4/4, plus 1 after the merge): the plan runs in a document; refusals at create and edit; undo/redo (op goes stale); project round-trip with no key for the default plan.\n- Existing suites unchanged and green: motion `turning_thread` and `turning_thread_cycle`; app `turning_thread`, `lathe_post_g76`, `lathe_field_tools` and `project_roundtrip`.\n- `clippy --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` passes except tests that already fail on main:\n  - the headless-GPU ui tests;\n  - `setup_stock_source::a_new_block_after_a_flip…` (#415);\n  - `swarf_pose_continuity` (2 tests; red on main, fixed by PR #351).\n\n## Not exercised (draft)\n- GUI check of the new Passes-tab rows.\n- **Posted G-code for non-default plans** (flank, constant area, allowance, spring passes) is new. It needs a lathe simulator or machine run before ready. Default plans post exactly as before.\n\nChangelog: Threading op: infeed method (radial / modified flank / alternating), decreasing-depth schedule, minimum depth, finish allowance and spring passes (#416)\n\nFixes #416\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
